1
00:00:35,064 --> 00:00:36,104
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,104 --> 00:00:37,134
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,134 --> 00:00:38,207
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:38,207 --> 00:00:40,400
[Episode 7]

5
00:00:42,896 --> 00:00:46,159
[Jaejae Noodles]

6
00:00:48,337 --> 00:00:50,609
- Going for a run again?
- Yeah.

7
00:00:50,609 --> 00:00:53,159
Why are you running in the middle of the night?

8
00:00:53,159 --> 00:00:55,051
So I don't run into him.

9
00:00:55,051 --> 00:00:56,438
You mean Soo Bin?

10
00:00:56,438 --> 00:00:59,026
Is that why you've been working from home?

11
00:00:59,026 --> 00:01:01,236
See? I told you.

12
00:01:01,236 --> 00:01:03,311
I knew I was right.

13
00:01:03,311 --> 00:01:05,354
Only a man knows...

14
00:01:05,354 --> 00:01:09,144
what's on another man's mind.

15
00:01:09,144 --> 00:01:11,413
Yeah! You're right!

16
00:01:11,413 --> 00:01:12,988
Dead right!

17
00:01:12,988 --> 00:01:14,872
- Darn it!
- Ugh...

18
00:01:15,766 --> 00:01:17,744
Ah, it's dead!

19
00:01:29,384 --> 00:01:32,180
[Revised Script for Gyeongseong Love Song]
<i>Sending the revised script.</i>

20
00:01:32,180 --> 00:01:34,837
Finally, I have an excuse to see her...

21
00:01:39,583 --> 00:01:41,010
I guess I still haven't moved on.

22
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:44,806
Mister, focus!

23
00:01:45,621 --> 00:01:48,043
- Here!
- Thank you.

24
00:01:51,566 --> 00:01:53,645
Give it to me. I'll open it for you.

25
00:01:55,411 --> 00:01:58,203
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

26
00:01:58,906 --> 00:02:02,273
- It came out!
- Oh, did you get it?

27
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:07,357
I really miss her...

28
00:02:07,357 --> 00:02:08,600
Who are you talking about?

29
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:11,845
- Oh... my colleague?
- Your colleague?

30
00:02:11,845 --> 00:02:13,589
Well...

31
00:02:13,589 --> 00:02:15,843
- My friend.
- I do know it.

32
00:02:15,843 --> 00:02:19,622
I just thought it was weird
to miss a colleague.

33
00:02:19,622 --> 00:02:20,873
Why is that weird?

34
00:02:20,873 --> 00:02:25,113
They say missing someone means you love them.

35
00:02:25,113 --> 00:02:28,837
It's hard to love a colleague, isn't it?

36
00:02:28,837 --> 00:02:31,859
You're pretty smart.

37
00:02:31,859 --> 00:02:33,836
- You take after your mom, don't you?
- Yep.

38
00:02:33,836 --> 00:02:38,856
They say I got my mom's brains
and my dad's face.

39
00:02:38,856 --> 00:02:40,353
Sounds about right.

40
00:02:40,353 --> 00:02:42,819
Kim Seong Chan! Daddy's here!

41
00:02:42,819 --> 00:02:44,364
Daddy!

42
00:02:44,364 --> 00:02:47,043
- Daddy!
- Oh, look who's here!

43
00:02:47,043 --> 00:02:49,301
Come here. Oh, my baby!

44
00:02:49,301 --> 00:02:51,308
- Did you have fun with him?
- Yes.

45
00:02:51,308 --> 00:02:53,035
Oh, dear... oh, my.

46
00:02:53,035 --> 00:02:54,433
Sorry about that.

47
00:02:54,433 --> 00:02:57,319
A big group came into Mom's restaurant.

48
00:02:57,319 --> 00:02:58,971
It's fine. It wasn't long.

49
00:02:58,971 --> 00:03:00,914
- I'll buy you a drink next time.
- It's fine.

50
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:03,079
Say goodbye, Seong Chan.

51
00:03:03,079 --> 00:03:06,734
- Yeah. Bye, Seung Chan.
- It's Seong Chan.

52
00:03:06,734 --> 00:03:11,049
Yeah, Seung Chan. See you next time.

53
00:03:11,049 --> 00:03:12,470
[Kim Seong Chan]

54
00:03:13,461 --> 00:03:16,096
Let's go, come here. Oh, dear.

55
00:03:16,096 --> 00:03:18,070
- Bye.
- Yeah, see you.

56
00:03:18,070 --> 00:03:20,117
- See you!
- Bye!

57
00:03:20,117 --> 00:03:24,401
Aw, you're such a cutie. Come on, let's go.

58
00:03:25,892 --> 00:03:27,965
He's such a good dad.

59
00:03:30,708 --> 00:03:32,464
Grandma, Mom!

60
00:03:32,464 --> 00:03:33,768
I brought twist donuts.

61
00:03:33,768 --> 00:03:36,021
We're already eating.

62
00:03:36,021 --> 00:03:38,396
Yi Jae stopped by earlier.

63
00:03:38,396 --> 00:03:40,571
Why haven't you two been hanging out lately?

64
00:03:40,571 --> 00:03:44,544
Oh, we've been working separately.

65
00:03:45,771 --> 00:03:48,309
By the way, what are you two doing?

66
00:03:48,309 --> 00:03:53,539
I'm studying for the written driver's test,
and Grandma's studying Korean!

67
00:03:53,539 --> 00:03:55,197
You're getting your driver's license?

68
00:03:55,197 --> 00:03:58,025
It's about time I learned to go places
on my own.

69
00:03:58,025 --> 00:04:00,115
And you'll go places with me too.

70
00:04:01,012 --> 00:04:03,119
I should teach you how to drive.

71
00:04:03,119 --> 00:04:05,582
They say you should never learn
driving from family.

72
00:04:05,582 --> 00:04:08,423
There! Look at this.

73
00:04:09,550 --> 00:04:11,842
[Park Jong Sun, Lee Hwa Yeon, Woo Soo Min]
I don't know everything yet,

74
00:04:11,842 --> 00:04:13,931
but I've got these memorized.

75
00:04:13,931 --> 00:04:16,687
Wow, even Mom's and my names?

76
00:04:16,687 --> 00:04:19,533
You'll be writing poetry before long.

77
00:04:20,686 --> 00:04:22,795
But...

78
00:04:22,795 --> 00:04:24,362
Like this... and like this.

79
00:04:24,362 --> 00:04:29,252
Oh, it's "bieup!" I knew that!

80
00:04:29,252 --> 00:04:31,251
"Bin."

81
00:04:31,251 --> 00:04:33,267
You never make mistakes.

82
00:04:33,267 --> 00:04:36,416
You must've gotten nervous
because Soo Bin's here.

83
00:04:36,416 --> 00:04:37,632
Oh, my...

84
00:04:37,632 --> 00:04:39,566
- "Bin!"
- "Bin."

85
00:04:39,566 --> 00:04:41,326
It's done, right?

86
00:04:54,398 --> 00:04:55,867
Mr. Kim?

87
00:04:55,867 --> 00:04:57,820
You can't just park here out
in the open like this.

88
00:04:57,820 --> 00:05:00,012
Madam's here, isn't she?

89
00:05:00,012 --> 00:05:02,165
Sir told me to bring her back.

90
00:05:02,165 --> 00:05:04,964
If he misses her that much,
tell him to come himself.

91
00:05:04,964 --> 00:05:06,935
Soo Bin!

92
00:05:16,975 --> 00:05:20,487
If you come again, I'll report you.

93
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:23,529
Soo Bin! Soo Bin...

94
00:05:23,529 --> 00:05:25,745
Okay, is everyone here?

95
00:05:25,745 --> 00:05:28,598
Please put it up on the screen...

96
00:05:28,598 --> 00:05:30,332
And here comes Mr. Game Changer.

97
00:05:30,332 --> 00:05:31,817
[Love Chain, The 7th Chain Mate Enters]

98
00:05:36,886 --> 00:05:40,372
- Oh, hello.
- Hello.

99
00:05:40,372 --> 00:05:42,726
Hello...

100
00:05:42,726 --> 00:05:45,313
Oh, me too...

101
00:05:45,313 --> 00:05:47,935
- Oh!
- Oh!

102
00:05:47,935 --> 00:05:50,221
- Please, have a seat wherever you'd like.
- Please have a seat.

103
00:05:50,221 --> 00:05:52,384
- Oh, sure.
- Yeah, where would you like to...

104
00:05:52,384 --> 00:05:55,068
Yeah, all the full shots look good,
and Camera 34 pan left...

105
00:05:55,068 --> 00:05:56,434
- and stay on the Game Changer.
- Sa Rang!

106
00:05:56,434 --> 00:06:00,372
Amazing! The vibe changed when he walked in.

107
00:06:00,372 --> 00:06:01,934
Isn't it amazing?

108
00:06:01,934 --> 00:06:04,769
Yes, yes. It looks good now...

109
00:06:04,769 --> 00:06:08,667
Let's get the men's group shots
and reactions next.

110
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:10,303
Yeah.

111
00:06:10,303 --> 00:06:12,435
- The Game Changer is getting a great reaction.
<i>- First impression...</i>

112
00:06:12,435 --> 00:06:13,818
- Yeah, good.
<i>- Well...</i>

113
00:06:13,818 --> 00:06:16,577
- The audio is picking up well, right?
<i>- For now, I'll just wait and see...</i>

114
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:20,600
Production team, do the interviews first,
then check the outdoor setup one more time.

115
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:24,178
- Yes, looks good.
<i>- There's sliced bread over there too.</i>

116
00:06:24,178 --> 00:06:26,665
<i>Grapes and egg tarts...</i>

117
00:06:39,212 --> 00:06:45,043
Boss, Yu Geon acts that way
because he feels guilty toward you.

118
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:48,920
And you act that way
because you love him. Right?

119
00:06:50,363 --> 00:06:53,196
Still, Yu Geon is pretty frustrating too.

120
00:06:53,196 --> 00:06:57,316
All he has to do is ask
my sister or Soo Bin to cast him.

121
00:06:57,316 --> 00:07:00,102
I wonder who he got that stubbornness from...

122
00:07:05,475 --> 00:07:07,344
He got it from me.

123
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:09,110
I was the same.

124
00:07:09,110 --> 00:07:11,787
All because of my stupid pride...

125
00:07:12,764 --> 00:07:15,314
I couldn't even ask anyone for help...

126
00:07:32,238 --> 00:07:34,984
Oh? Mister! Hello.

127
00:07:34,984 --> 00:07:37,610
Hey, Soo Bin. It's been a while.

128
00:07:37,610 --> 00:07:41,424
Uh... is Yi Jae here with you?

129
00:07:41,424 --> 00:07:44,489
No, it's just me right now.

130
00:07:44,489 --> 00:07:47,052
Oh, I see...

131
00:07:47,052 --> 00:07:50,822
- Would you like to come in for a moment?
- No, never mind.

132
00:07:50,822 --> 00:07:53,916
Well, the reason I'm here is...

133
00:07:53,916 --> 00:07:57,635
I wanted you and Yi Jae to take a look at this.

134
00:07:57,635 --> 00:07:58,670
What's this?

135
00:07:58,670 --> 00:08:00,797
Don't feel pressured. Got it?

136
00:08:00,797 --> 00:08:03,440
- Oh...
- See you.

137
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:07,372
- No, sir, this...
- Yeah, yeah. Go on inside.

138
00:08:15,797 --> 00:08:16,853
[Yu Geon's Dream]

139
00:08:16,853 --> 00:08:19,604
[Bus No. 31 (Mail Carrier)]
[Letter from That Day (Post Office Employee 3)]

140
00:08:19,604 --> 00:08:22,482
[Witness for the Shadows (Court Clerk)]
[Fishing King (Student 2)]

141
00:08:25,572 --> 00:08:29,064
You've really worked hard, Sim Yu Geon.

142
00:08:29,064 --> 00:08:30,522
[Sending the revised script]

143
00:08:30,522 --> 00:08:31,805
[Thank you]
[Thank you for your hard work]

144
00:08:31,805 --> 00:08:34,483
He read it, but didn't say a word.

145
00:08:35,739 --> 00:08:36,760
[Woo Soo Bin]

146
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:40,171
Why's he calling?

147
00:08:40,171 --> 00:08:41,735
No...

148
00:08:42,484 --> 00:08:44,337
It'll look like I've been
waiting for him to call.

149
00:08:44,337 --> 00:08:46,696
But I have! Right?

150
00:08:46,696 --> 00:08:49,023
I've been waiting for feedback!

151
00:08:53,096 --> 00:08:54,673
Yeah?

152
00:08:55,595 --> 00:08:57,224
Yeah, now?

153
00:08:57,224 --> 00:08:58,629
Oh, to your studio?

154
00:08:58,629 --> 00:09:01,729
Oh, now? Well...

155
00:09:01,729 --> 00:09:03,873
It might take a while...

156
00:09:03,873 --> 00:09:07,794
Okay, see you later. Yeah.

157
00:09:08,856 --> 00:09:11,318
That was incredibly natural.

158
00:09:13,336 --> 00:09:14,985
Well...

159
00:09:14,985 --> 00:09:18,440
Being colleagues isn't so hard after all!

160
00:09:27,807 --> 00:09:30,336
Oh, I was wondering who it was.

161
00:09:30,336 --> 00:09:33,035
- You could've just come in.
- It's called manners.

162
00:09:33,035 --> 00:09:34,754
Yeah...

163
00:09:36,431 --> 00:09:37,792
Oh...

164
00:09:37,792 --> 00:09:39,599
you...

165
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:42,270
Well...

166
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:44,979
- I'll go this way.
- Oh, okay.

167
00:09:49,792 --> 00:09:51,824
[10 Reasons Contract Marriage Is Dangerous]
<i>Go with Plan B!</i>

168
00:10:00,644 --> 00:10:03,559
Wow... even his latest drama is here?

169
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,935
Mister gave you all this?

170
00:10:04,935 --> 00:10:06,494
It's a little over an hour long.

171
00:10:06,494 --> 00:10:08,932
Has it already been an hour?

172
00:10:08,932 --> 00:10:10,707
Time flies.

173
00:10:10,707 --> 00:10:14,179
Waiting for you felt longer...

174
00:10:14,179 --> 00:10:15,678
Huh?

175
00:10:15,678 --> 00:10:17,556
Oh, well...

176
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:23,257
Well, I guess it's because
Yu Geon's such a good actor.

177
00:10:25,013 --> 00:10:28,354
Exactly... that's what I meant.

178
00:10:28,354 --> 00:10:30,589
Then maybe there's something
Yu Geon could do...

179
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:34,475
- Even a small role...
- Yeah, even a small role would be good.

180
00:10:36,056 --> 00:10:37,940
- No, I don't want to give him one.
- Huh?

181
00:10:37,940 --> 00:10:41,009
I don't want to throw him scraps like,
"Here, take this."

182
00:10:41,009 --> 00:10:43,373
It's disrespectful to Yu Geon.

183
00:10:43,373 --> 00:10:45,175
Let him audition.

184
00:10:45,175 --> 00:10:47,613
But if I bring him in,
he'll probably refuse to come.

185
00:10:47,613 --> 00:10:50,474
If he gets it, it'll feel awkward.
If he doesn't, he'll be disappointed.

186
00:10:50,474 --> 00:10:53,104
Then it would be better
to reach out through his agency.

187
00:10:53,104 --> 00:10:54,490
He doesn't have an agency.

188
00:10:54,490 --> 00:10:56,543
What? Then he's been doing all this on his own?

189
00:10:56,543 --> 00:10:59,246
Having an agency makes a huge difference.

190
00:10:59,246 --> 00:11:01,827
You don't even get
the same audition opportunities.

191
00:11:01,827 --> 00:11:03,909
Oh, jeez...

192
00:11:03,909 --> 00:11:05,585
I don't get it.

193
00:11:05,585 --> 00:11:09,450
Does he think actors with that face
and that level of talent are common?

194
00:11:09,450 --> 00:11:11,681
Uh... well...

195
00:11:14,611 --> 00:11:15,613
What?

196
00:11:15,613 --> 00:11:20,402
You've always loved his face.
Enough to make me jealous.

197
00:11:20,402 --> 00:11:22,621
I was the jealous one.

198
00:11:22,621 --> 00:11:25,783
You were the one who said
Yu Geon has a face the camera can't resist.

199
00:11:25,783 --> 00:11:28,994
When did I say that? I filmed you a lot more.

200
00:11:28,994 --> 00:11:31,403
- Huh?
- Oh...

201
00:11:31,403 --> 00:11:35,675
Well, that makes sense. We were dating...

202
00:11:35,675 --> 00:11:36,957
Oh...

203
00:11:36,957 --> 00:11:38,944
That's all in the past.

204
00:11:38,944 --> 00:11:42,265
- I just can't resist filming beautiful...
- Huh?

205
00:11:42,265 --> 00:11:43,660
Oh...

206
00:11:49,939 --> 00:11:51,852
Well, then... I should go.

207
00:11:51,852 --> 00:11:52,959
Where are you going?

208
00:11:52,959 --> 00:11:57,432
- Huh? What?
- We still have to go over the revised script.

209
00:11:57,432 --> 00:11:58,973
Oh.

210
00:12:03,745 --> 00:12:05,856
Here? O-over there?

211
00:12:05,856 --> 00:12:07,772
- Yeah.
- Should we do it there?

212
00:12:09,073 --> 00:12:10,665
Here? Oh...

213
00:12:17,889 --> 00:12:20,727
[An Su Hui]
[Sim Yu Geon]

214
00:12:24,724 --> 00:12:27,492
<i>Why are you offering me a contract like this?</i>

215
00:12:28,114 --> 00:12:30,706
<i>It seems like I have nothing to lose.</i>

216
00:12:31,821 --> 00:12:34,618
<i>You've already lost the most important thing.</i>

217
00:12:34,618 --> 00:12:37,142
<i>I bought your heart.</i>

218
00:12:37,142 --> 00:12:39,701
<i>So you'll never fall in love with Ha Na.</i>

219
00:12:39,701 --> 00:12:43,142
<i>- I never had those feelings to begin with.
- Of course, you don't. I took them.</i>

220
00:12:43,142 --> 00:12:45,437
<i>And you'd better keep it that way.</i>

221
00:12:46,671 --> 00:12:48,148
<i>Isn't it funny?</i>

222
00:12:48,148 --> 00:12:53,344
<i>That a single piece of paper can bind
both your body and your heart.</i>

223
00:13:00,842 --> 00:13:02,892
Wow...

224
00:13:05,673 --> 00:13:07,227
Wow...

225
00:13:07,227 --> 00:13:11,032
I like people like you, who show results
right away when you invest in them.

226
00:13:11,032 --> 00:13:13,900
Makes spending money worthwhile. Get in.

227
00:13:37,368 --> 00:13:41,227
No. You should sit next to me. Right here.

228
00:13:41,843 --> 00:13:43,417
Oh...

229
00:13:48,606 --> 00:13:50,803
Is someone else joining us?

230
00:13:52,674 --> 00:13:55,637
- Oh.
- Oh, you're already here.

231
00:13:59,493 --> 00:14:01,386
Sim Yu Geon!

232
00:14:02,739 --> 00:14:04,412
Soo Bin.

233
00:14:05,628 --> 00:14:08,596
Oh, you know each other?

234
00:14:08,596 --> 00:14:10,838
Perfect.

235
00:14:10,838 --> 00:14:13,890
Maybe we'll make it to the gym
before it closes after all.

236
00:14:14,963 --> 00:14:18,653
Looks like you're really happy
to see him here, huh, Ian?

237
00:14:18,653 --> 00:14:20,307
What do you want?

238
00:14:20,307 --> 00:14:24,874
What does it look like?
I want him to play Moo Gyeom.

239
00:14:30,330 --> 00:14:31,818
What?

240
00:14:33,705 --> 00:14:36,204
You've really outdone yourself.

241
00:14:36,204 --> 00:14:39,003
First you created an audition
that wasn't even planned,

242
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:40,884
and now you're telling us who to cast?

243
00:14:40,884 --> 00:14:43,025
As the lead, no less?

244
00:14:44,664 --> 00:14:48,271
Director Ian, don't block the doorway.
Come sit down.

245
00:14:48,271 --> 00:14:50,111
You too.

246
00:14:51,872 --> 00:14:54,485
Sim Yu Geon, come outside.

247
00:15:00,942 --> 00:15:03,052
Aren't you coming out?

248
00:15:14,673 --> 00:15:16,970
Looks like we're not making it
to the gym today.

249
00:15:24,001 --> 00:15:26,295
What are you doing here?

250
00:15:26,295 --> 00:15:29,787
Yi Jae was even hesitant
to suggest you audition.

251
00:15:29,787 --> 00:15:32,436
I guess we worried for nothing.

252
00:15:32,436 --> 00:15:35,331
You should've just asked Yi Jae or me.

253
00:15:35,331 --> 00:15:38,229
That would've been much easier.

254
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:43,025
This is easier than becoming
a burden to the people I care about.

255
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:45,549
So this is what you chose instead?

256
00:15:45,549 --> 00:15:48,396
I didn't know I'd run into you.

257
00:15:49,096 --> 00:15:50,832
I'm sorry.

258
00:15:53,448 --> 00:15:55,162
If you were going to get in
through connections anyway,

259
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:58,022
you should've done it back
when you were young enough to be naive.

260
00:15:58,022 --> 00:16:00,693
After everything you've put yourself through...

261
00:16:01,361 --> 00:16:03,024
now, of all times?

262
00:16:03,694 --> 00:16:05,743
What do you know?

263
00:16:05,743 --> 00:16:07,653
You have no idea what it took
for me to make it this far.

264
00:16:07,653 --> 00:16:10,324
So don't act like you know
what I've been through.

265
00:16:10,324 --> 00:16:12,911
You think I should've done it when I was naive?

266
00:16:14,773 --> 00:16:18,074
I did the best I could back then...

267
00:16:18,994 --> 00:16:21,514
and this is the best I can do now.

268
00:16:22,712 --> 00:16:24,165
Yeah.

269
00:16:25,099 --> 00:16:26,302
But...

270
00:16:26,302 --> 00:16:28,677
look at yourself in the mirror.

271
00:16:28,677 --> 00:16:31,666
Does this look like
the face of someone doing his best?

272
00:16:33,732 --> 00:16:35,508
Sim Yu Geon.

273
00:16:36,117 --> 00:16:40,563
I may not have liked you that much,
but I always thought you had a certain charm.

274
00:16:41,196 --> 00:16:44,852
But, right now... you're not.

275
00:16:59,214 --> 00:17:00,808
Ian!

276
00:17:01,935 --> 00:17:03,468
Wait!

277
00:17:03,468 --> 00:17:05,159
Hey, you...

278
00:17:07,095 --> 00:17:09,240
You're just leaving like this?

279
00:17:09,240 --> 00:17:12,558
Calm down and hear me out.

280
00:17:12,558 --> 00:17:14,719
You crossed the line too.

281
00:17:14,719 --> 00:17:18,223
At least back then with Oh Ha Na,
you had the decency to go behind my back.

282
00:17:18,223 --> 00:17:22,342
He was going to audition anyway.
And isn't he someone you know?

283
00:17:22,342 --> 00:17:26,730
- Isn't this a good thing?
- Exactly. So you took away his chance.

284
00:17:26,730 --> 00:17:29,721
Without this, he could've earned
some other role on his own.

285
00:17:29,721 --> 00:17:33,405
Sometimes you give up one thing
to gain another.

286
00:17:33,405 --> 00:17:35,502
You have to protect Yi Jae, right?

287
00:17:37,201 --> 00:17:40,780
What does Yi Jae have to do with this?

288
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:45,664
What we need to do here is cast Sim Yu Geon...

289
00:17:45,664 --> 00:17:47,853
and protect Yi Jae.

290
00:17:47,853 --> 00:17:50,869
- In Uk!
- Ian, wake up.

291
00:17:50,869 --> 00:17:54,607
I don't care how many awards you've won
or how successful your debut was...

292
00:17:54,607 --> 00:17:56,409
This is only your second project.

293
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:59,294
It's a period romance
that's already hard to finance...

294
00:17:59,294 --> 00:18:02,877
and co-directed
with an unproven newcomer. Hey...

295
00:18:02,877 --> 00:18:04,691
You're already getting
almost everything you wanted.

296
00:18:04,691 --> 00:18:07,098
Can't you give up this one thing?

297
00:18:10,758 --> 00:18:13,576
Without CEO An,

298
00:18:13,576 --> 00:18:16,836
we never would've gotten this far.

299
00:18:17,437 --> 00:18:20,630
Don't forget where we came from. Okay?

300
00:18:20,630 --> 00:18:22,360
You're right.

301
00:18:23,237 --> 00:18:25,740
You should've told me from the start...

302
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:27,878
that people like us couldn't do this, Mr. Seo.

303
00:18:27,878 --> 00:18:30,761
You said it had to be this project!

304
00:18:30,761 --> 00:18:34,413
What was I supposed to do?
You said it was your dream!

305
00:18:38,112 --> 00:18:40,933
You were only 22...

306
00:18:40,933 --> 00:18:42,951
wandering around with nowhere to live,

307
00:18:42,951 --> 00:18:44,963
carrying nothing but that script
when you came to me.

308
00:18:44,963 --> 00:18:47,713
I still remember that day.

309
00:18:49,549 --> 00:18:53,196
Just like you're trying to keep
the promise you made to Yi Jae, I'm...

310
00:18:53,196 --> 00:18:54,919
I'm just trying to keep
the promise I made to you.

311
00:18:54,919 --> 00:18:58,497
But I'm not capable of doing more yet,
so this is the best I can do.

312
00:19:04,173 --> 00:19:06,073
I'm sorry.

313
00:19:07,305 --> 00:19:10,439
I'm sorry... sorry, Ian.

314
00:19:28,167 --> 00:19:31,497
Come on in. The food's getting cold.

315
00:19:38,382 --> 00:19:40,371
Director Woo.

316
00:19:40,371 --> 00:19:42,709
I'm sure CEO Seo explained it.

317
00:19:43,411 --> 00:19:45,318
Give him the role...

318
00:19:45,318 --> 00:19:48,669
or drop Ju Yi Jae.

319
00:19:51,526 --> 00:19:54,645
You're set on backing Sim Yu Geon,

320
00:19:54,645 --> 00:19:57,478
and I'm set on protecting Ju Yi Jae...

321
00:19:58,101 --> 00:20:00,743
Doesn't that already answer the question?

322
00:20:00,743 --> 00:20:02,094
I like how quick you are.

323
00:20:02,094 --> 00:20:04,914
Let's make one thing clear.

324
00:20:06,109 --> 00:20:07,882
This film...

325
00:20:08,594 --> 00:20:11,282
won't fall apart just because we lose
one investor like you, CEO An,

326
00:20:11,282 --> 00:20:15,713
but it cannot be made
without Director Ju Yi Jae.

327
00:20:15,713 --> 00:20:17,932
You decided to invest because of her script,

328
00:20:17,932 --> 00:20:22,247
so I'd appreciate it...
if you stopped telling us to keep or cut her.

329
00:20:25,413 --> 00:20:30,102
I only looked because it was
your next project. Otherwise...

330
00:20:30,102 --> 00:20:33,041
would it have ever made it onto my desk?

331
00:20:34,150 --> 00:20:37,780
Anyway, I got the answer I wanted,
so I'll be going now.

332
00:20:37,780 --> 00:20:40,386
Oh... you're leaving already?

333
00:20:40,386 --> 00:20:41,811
He has boxing practice.

334
00:20:41,811 --> 00:20:44,115
Even if we leave now,
he'll only get an hour in.

335
00:20:44,115 --> 00:20:45,789
Oh...

336
00:20:46,753 --> 00:20:48,787
What are you doing? Aren't you coming?

337
00:20:48,787 --> 00:20:50,452
Goodbye.

338
00:20:52,695 --> 00:20:54,609
Oh, right!

339
00:20:54,609 --> 00:20:57,278
I heard you're already
looking for a top actress.

340
00:20:57,278 --> 00:21:00,491
Since I saved you the trouble of
finding your male lead,

341
00:21:00,491 --> 00:21:05,772
why not spend that time
finding the perfect female lead instead?

342
00:21:21,219 --> 00:21:23,965
- Oh? You're getting back from work, In Uk?
- Yeah.

343
00:21:23,965 --> 00:21:26,109
Aren't you all dying to know
what In Uk does for a living?

344
00:21:26,109 --> 00:21:27,324
- Yeah.
- Right.

345
00:21:27,324 --> 00:21:30,300
Go change and come join us!
We were just about to play Truth or Dare!

346
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:32,550
Oh... I'm exhausted.

347
00:21:32,550 --> 00:21:34,760
Have a good time.

348
00:21:35,989 --> 00:21:38,131
It's understandable to be tired...

349
00:21:38,131 --> 00:21:39,155
That's a shame.

350
00:21:39,155 --> 00:21:41,297
- Right.
- Right.

351
00:21:42,323 --> 00:21:46,161
Those two are heading to the terrace!
Stay on them!

352
00:22:10,589 --> 00:22:12,500
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

353
00:22:12,500 --> 00:22:14,809
<i>You look tired.</i>

354
00:22:56,873 --> 00:23:00,510
<i>Keep what we talked about earlier
a secret from Yi Jae.</i>

355
00:23:14,908 --> 00:23:17,311
You came, Yu Geon?

356
00:23:17,311 --> 00:23:21,214
What? Why do you look so cool today?

357
00:23:21,214 --> 00:23:23,596
Were you playing the handsome lead?

358
00:23:24,393 --> 00:23:26,394
Why are you here?

359
00:23:27,074 --> 00:23:29,439
Well... you weren't replying,

360
00:23:29,439 --> 00:23:33,447
and your motorcycle was outside,
so I thought you were home.

361
00:23:34,460 --> 00:23:37,716
By the way, is something wrong?

362
00:23:37,716 --> 00:23:40,395
You look exhausted.

363
00:23:40,395 --> 00:23:43,193
- I asked why you came.
- Oh!

364
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:46,554
Give me your hand.

365
00:23:46,554 --> 00:23:48,816
Come on.

366
00:23:56,624 --> 00:24:00,348
Ta-da! I snuck this out of my mom's drawer.

367
00:24:00,348 --> 00:24:03,256
My voyage has officially begun.

368
00:24:03,256 --> 00:24:04,914
I did well, right?

369
00:24:09,551 --> 00:24:12,873
I hate...

370
00:24:12,873 --> 00:24:15,229
when you show up like this.

371
00:24:20,342 --> 00:24:21,819
Are you mad?

372
00:24:21,819 --> 00:24:23,443
Because I came without telling you?

373
00:24:23,443 --> 00:24:25,068
I'm sorry.

374
00:24:25,068 --> 00:24:28,308
- Next time I'll...
- Let's stop being friends too.

375
00:24:30,206 --> 00:24:32,998
How could we ever be friends?

376
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:37,421
Friends are people
who belong in the same world.

377
00:24:39,312 --> 00:24:40,918
Then...

378
00:24:42,684 --> 00:24:46,809
What have we been until now?

379
00:24:48,987 --> 00:24:52,513
Oh Ha Na... and Extra No. 1.

380
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:57,416
Please leave.

381
00:25:18,605 --> 00:25:23,880
[Expiration date: Ten thousand years]

382
00:25:51,743 --> 00:25:53,367
[Open Frame Works, Film Production]

383
00:26:00,357 --> 00:26:04,110
Wow... my stick-figure storyboard
turned into this?

384
00:26:04,110 --> 00:26:07,717
- Who drew these storyboards?
- Director Ian did them himself.

385
00:26:07,717 --> 00:26:09,351
Oh, he... I mean,

386
00:26:09,351 --> 00:26:11,816
Director Woo even draws his own storyboards?

387
00:26:11,816 --> 00:26:17,318
Yeah. He doesn't have a storyboard artist.
He usually draws the storyboards himself.

388
00:26:17,318 --> 00:26:21,452
No wonder... it was exactly how I imagined it.

389
00:26:25,310 --> 00:26:27,090
You're here.

390
00:26:27,090 --> 00:26:30,823
- Jenny, could you give us a minute?
- Yeah.

391
00:26:38,758 --> 00:26:42,140
- What's up?
- We're going to discuss this in the meeting...

392
00:26:42,140 --> 00:26:44,269
but I thought you should know beforehand.

393
00:26:44,269 --> 00:26:46,428
What is it?

394
00:26:46,428 --> 00:26:49,111
Sim Yu Geon has been...

395
00:26:49,111 --> 00:26:51,757
cast as Moo Gyeom. It's official.

396
00:26:51,757 --> 00:26:55,811
Yu Geon? That Sim Yu Geon I know? How?

397
00:26:55,811 --> 00:26:59,304
Wasn't he supposed to audition?
Did it already happen?

398
00:26:59,304 --> 00:27:02,162
Turns out Yu Geon signed with Topline.

399
00:27:03,519 --> 00:27:07,940
And as you know,
CEO An is our business partner...

400
00:27:07,940 --> 00:27:10,543
Sim Yu Geon signed with them?

401
00:27:10,543 --> 00:27:12,291
They must see a lot of potential in him.

402
00:27:12,291 --> 00:27:15,778
A company that big doesn't back just anyone.

403
00:27:15,778 --> 00:27:20,525
Wow... what's gotten into Yu Geon?
Best betrayal ever.

404
00:27:21,445 --> 00:27:25,114
- You look really happy.
- Of course I am! This is amazing!

405
00:27:25,114 --> 00:27:27,331
But that's so fascinating.

406
00:27:27,331 --> 00:27:30,603
I guess when it's meant to happen,
it finds a way.

407
00:27:30,603 --> 00:27:33,506
As long as you're happy... it's fine.

408
00:27:33,506 --> 00:27:36,209
Oh, sorry.

409
00:27:36,209 --> 00:27:38,748
I was only thinking about myself.
Are you okay with this?

410
00:27:38,748 --> 00:27:41,989
We were going to have Yu Geon audition anyway.

411
00:27:41,989 --> 00:27:44,877
- I'm happy too.
- Oh...

412
00:27:51,193 --> 00:27:52,883
Hello.

413
00:27:52,883 --> 00:27:54,761
You're here.

414
00:27:54,761 --> 00:27:57,838
- Take care.
- Good work.

415
00:28:04,581 --> 00:28:07,066
- Good work today.
- Good work.

416
00:28:07,066 --> 00:28:08,856
Good work today.

417
00:28:09,557 --> 00:28:13,591
Oh. Hey, Sim Yu Geon!

418
00:28:20,234 --> 00:28:25,406
Hey! Why the long face?
We should be throwing you a celebration!

419
00:28:26,238 --> 00:28:28,833
- I'm sorry, Yi Jae.
- What are you sorry for?

420
00:28:28,833 --> 00:28:30,814
I'm grateful you're playing our Moo Gyeom.

421
00:28:30,814 --> 00:28:34,475
I know what this film means to you...

422
00:28:34,475 --> 00:28:36,888
I shouldn't have let it happen like this.

423
00:28:37,529 --> 00:28:39,133
Yu Geon,

424
00:28:39,133 --> 00:28:41,280
that's life, you know.

425
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:44,568
Sometimes a meteor just drops
right in front of you.

426
00:28:44,568 --> 00:28:47,636
You wonder if it could really belong to you,

427
00:28:47,636 --> 00:28:49,890
but if you pick it up, then it's yours.

428
00:28:49,890 --> 00:28:52,842
You grabbed this opportunity,
so stop shrinking away from it.

429
00:28:52,842 --> 00:28:55,355
Our Moo Gyeom isn't that kind of person.

430
00:28:57,949 --> 00:29:01,087
- Yi Jae...
- I'm not just trying to comfort you.

431
00:29:01,087 --> 00:29:04,435
I don't want you thinking you got this
only because of CEO An.

432
00:29:04,435 --> 00:29:06,292
Do Soo Bin and I look like pushovers?

433
00:29:06,292 --> 00:29:09,661
Do we seem like the type to say yes
to something we absolutely hate?

434
00:29:09,661 --> 00:29:11,880
No, but...

435
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:21,138
Seriously, what's gotten into you?
Do I have to knock some sense into you?

436
00:29:24,713 --> 00:29:26,346
Yi Jae...

437
00:29:27,522 --> 00:29:32,713
I don't think I can be part of your film
while keeping this from you.

438
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:37,393
<i>The door is opening.</i>

439
00:29:47,315 --> 00:29:50,030
<i>Soo Bin told me not to say anything.</i>

440
00:29:52,436 --> 00:29:56,195
<i>But... CEO An made a deal.</i>

441
00:29:56,195 --> 00:29:58,792
<i>She said if they didn't cast me as the lead,</i>

442
00:30:00,277 --> 00:30:02,991
<i>she'd remove you as director.</i>

443
00:30:02,991 --> 00:30:06,838
<i>Soo Bin accepted me to protect you.</i>

444
00:30:14,960 --> 00:30:17,003
Hey! Director Woo!

445
00:30:17,766 --> 00:30:19,067
I thought you went home.

446
00:30:19,067 --> 00:30:21,200
You should eat while you work.
I brought gimbap.

447
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:24,400
I was getting hungry. Thanks.

448
00:30:33,234 --> 00:30:36,081
Did you meet with Yu Geon?

449
00:30:36,081 --> 00:30:38,644
Oh... yeah.

450
00:30:38,644 --> 00:30:44,019
He looked like a soaked puppy,
so I gave him a good talking-to!

451
00:30:44,019 --> 00:30:48,804
- He's talented. He'll do a great job.
- Yeah.

452
00:30:48,804 --> 00:30:50,912
I'll enjoy it.

453
00:30:50,912 --> 00:30:53,075
Thank you.

454
00:30:53,075 --> 00:30:54,996
Oh, it looks so good.

455
00:30:55,844 --> 00:30:59,290
[Yu Geon's Dream]

456
00:31:09,299 --> 00:31:12,496
<i>I heard your father left this for Woo Soo Bin.</i>

457
00:31:12,496 --> 00:31:14,270
<i>He asked him to look after you, Yu Geon.</i>

458
00:31:14,270 --> 00:31:16,827
<i>If you were going to get in
through connections anyway,</i>

459
00:31:16,827 --> 00:31:19,757
<i>you should've done it back
when you were young enough to be naive.</i>

460
00:31:19,757 --> 00:31:22,861
<i>After everything you've put yourself through...
now, of all times?</i>

461
00:31:22,861 --> 00:31:25,465
<i>You've already lost the most important thing.</i>

462
00:31:25,465 --> 00:31:27,776
<i>I bought your heart.</i>

463
00:31:27,776 --> 00:31:29,835
<i>So you'll never fall in love with Ha Na.</i>

464
00:31:29,835 --> 00:31:33,627
<i>Ta-da! I snuck this out of my mom's drawer.</i>

465
00:31:33,627 --> 00:31:36,507
<i>My voyage has officially begun.</i>

466
00:31:36,507 --> 00:31:38,407
<i>I did well, right?</i>

467
00:32:05,030 --> 00:32:06,468
[Actor Sim Yu Geon]

468
00:32:11,573 --> 00:32:14,593
Why? Did something happen?

469
00:32:15,553 --> 00:32:17,059
<i>Dad...</i>

470
00:32:17,651 --> 00:32:20,460
Yeah, why? Did something happen?

471
00:32:22,113 --> 00:32:25,405
<i>I got... cast.</i>

472
00:32:25,405 --> 00:32:28,608
<i>I'm the lead in a movie.</i>

473
00:32:34,338 --> 00:32:36,041
Really?

474
00:32:37,970 --> 00:32:40,225
Then why do you sound like that?

475
00:32:43,277 --> 00:32:45,177
<i>Because I'm happy.</i>

476
00:32:48,414 --> 00:32:50,137
Yeah?

477
00:32:50,137 --> 00:32:51,519
Good. You've worked hard.

478
00:32:51,519 --> 00:32:53,085
Let's hang up.

479
00:32:53,991 --> 00:32:55,541
<i>Dad!</i>

480
00:32:58,658 --> 00:33:00,558
<i>Thank you.</i>

481
00:33:30,495 --> 00:33:33,517
Are you sure you're okay staying at my place?

482
00:33:33,517 --> 00:33:36,516
If you ask me one more time, that'll make ten.

483
00:33:36,516 --> 00:33:39,058
Stop asking. I'm really fine.

484
00:33:39,058 --> 00:33:43,688
I can't believe someone like you
would come to such a humble place...

485
00:33:43,688 --> 00:33:47,654
When I shoot overseas,
I've stayed in much worse places.

486
00:33:47,654 --> 00:33:51,134
Give me a sleeping bag
and I can even sleep outside.

487
00:33:55,478 --> 00:33:58,521
I'll put the suitcase in quickly.

488
00:34:11,738 --> 00:34:14,101
Are you going somewhere?

489
00:34:14,101 --> 00:34:15,571
The New York shoot isn't until next week.

490
00:34:15,571 --> 00:34:20,914
You know next week's schedule,
but not that my contract ended?

491
00:34:20,914 --> 00:34:23,891
Since when have we ever worked
by the contract dates?

492
00:34:23,891 --> 00:34:26,039
I'm going independent.

493
00:34:26,039 --> 00:34:27,158
I'm not renewing.

494
00:34:27,158 --> 00:34:29,547
- What, are you retiring?
- No.

495
00:34:29,547 --> 00:34:31,700
Why do you assume I'm quitting?

496
00:34:31,700 --> 00:34:33,537
Because you've never wanted to do it.

497
00:34:33,537 --> 00:34:38,035
I never even got the chance to find out!

498
00:34:38,673 --> 00:34:41,619
From now on, I'm living my own life.

499
00:34:41,619 --> 00:34:45,061
- Did you get everything loaded, Chae Yeon?
- Yeah.

500
00:34:46,858 --> 00:34:49,666
Thank you for everything, CEO An.

501
00:34:51,945 --> 00:34:54,389
Is this because of Sim Yu Geon?

502
00:34:55,890 --> 00:35:00,499
You've been acting like a teenager.
Is it because of him?

503
00:35:00,499 --> 00:35:05,468
Jeez... how could you
fall for someone like him?

504
00:35:05,468 --> 00:35:07,222
Go see a therapist instead!

505
00:35:07,222 --> 00:35:08,354
- Mom!
- What!

506
00:35:08,354 --> 00:35:13,121
It's because of you!
You make me feel like I can't breathe!

507
00:35:13,121 --> 00:35:14,865
And you already dug into
Yu Geon's background again?

508
00:35:14,865 --> 00:35:18,763
Oh, jeez... what do you take me for?

509
00:35:18,763 --> 00:35:23,045
You think I only look into people's pasts?
I look at their futures too.

510
00:35:23,045 --> 00:35:26,726
So stop acting up
and go clear your head for a couple of days.

511
00:35:26,726 --> 00:35:28,593
Gangneung should do.

512
00:35:28,593 --> 00:35:32,323
Chae Yeon, use the company card!
And don't let Ha Na eat sweets!

513
00:35:32,323 --> 00:35:34,068
Yes...

514
00:35:39,009 --> 00:35:42,503
Director Kang, announce Ha Na's hiatus.

515
00:35:42,503 --> 00:35:45,809
The reason? Make something.

516
00:35:53,177 --> 00:35:55,651
Ha Na, do we really have to go this far?

517
00:35:55,651 --> 00:35:57,338
Huh? That's Jaden.

518
00:35:57,338 --> 00:35:59,123
Who's that? Should we stop him?

519
00:35:59,123 --> 00:36:00,961
No, pass.

520
00:36:00,961 --> 00:36:02,758
He's a CEO now.

521
00:36:02,758 --> 00:36:05,490
CEOs can't be trusted as my mom can...

522
00:36:05,490 --> 00:36:07,092
Pass on the CEO!

523
00:36:07,092 --> 00:36:09,574
Ha Na! That's Director Ian!

524
00:36:09,574 --> 00:36:12,235
- Should we stop him? Should I go now?
- No, no!

525
00:36:12,235 --> 00:36:14,594
He's the last person we should approach.

526
00:36:14,594 --> 00:36:19,518
But he's directing "Gyeongseong Love Song."
Then who are we supposed to ask?

527
00:36:19,518 --> 00:36:21,007
Huh?

528
00:36:21,638 --> 00:36:23,347
That person!

529
00:36:23,980 --> 00:36:26,112
Ha Na, wait...

530
00:36:35,732 --> 00:36:37,872
Director Ju Yi Jae.

531
00:36:40,777 --> 00:36:42,562
Oh Ha Na?

532
00:36:44,486 --> 00:36:46,539
But how do you know me?

533
00:36:46,539 --> 00:36:49,725
I used to watch "Here comes Yi Jae."

534
00:36:49,725 --> 00:36:52,881
We even met at that
department store event. Right?

535
00:36:53,557 --> 00:36:57,550
Isn't this what you call... fate?

536
00:36:57,550 --> 00:36:59,147
Fate?

537
00:37:00,641 --> 00:37:03,770
Oh, what was it you wanted to tell me earlier?

538
00:37:04,675 --> 00:37:06,996
Please give me the script for
"Gyeongseong Love Song," Director.

539
00:37:06,996 --> 00:37:11,071
Oh, I thought a copy
was already sent to CEO An.

540
00:37:11,071 --> 00:37:14,587
Exactly! I should've stolen it then!

541
00:37:14,587 --> 00:37:16,009
Pardon?

542
00:37:16,648 --> 00:37:21,043
I really want to be in this film, Director.

543
00:37:21,043 --> 00:37:23,889
I've never wanted anything like this before.

544
00:37:23,889 --> 00:37:26,206
- Really?
- Yes...

545
00:37:27,469 --> 00:37:28,637
Can you hear her?

546
00:37:28,637 --> 00:37:31,997
Nan Young is alive inside me.

547
00:37:31,997 --> 00:37:33,437
Yes, I can hear her.

548
00:37:33,437 --> 00:37:35,832
Yes. I'll get it to you. How should I send it?

549
00:37:35,832 --> 00:37:38,321
Through your manager?

550
00:37:39,685 --> 00:37:42,167
Put your number in, Yi Jae.

551
00:37:42,167 --> 00:37:45,002
"Yi Jae..." "Yi Jae?"

552
00:37:45,002 --> 00:37:48,270
Is Oh Ha Na seriously asking for
my number right now?

553
00:37:48,270 --> 00:37:49,876
But...

554
00:37:49,876 --> 00:37:53,302
let's keep today our little secret.

555
00:37:53,302 --> 00:37:55,880
- Yes.
- Shh!

556
00:37:56,984 --> 00:37:59,440
[An Yoo Jeong]

557
00:37:59,440 --> 00:38:00,751
[Lim Min Ju]

558
00:38:00,751 --> 00:38:04,487
As expected, top stars
are booked two projects ahead.

559
00:38:04,487 --> 00:38:08,358
At least Actress Lim Min Ju might be
available if schedules work out.

560
00:38:08,358 --> 00:38:11,334
Well... what about Oh Ha Na?

561
00:38:12,063 --> 00:38:16,595
Oh... I heard she's in talks for another film.

562
00:38:16,595 --> 00:38:20,044
An article came out a few days ago saying
she's taking a break from acting.

563
00:38:20,044 --> 00:38:21,641
Really?

564
00:38:24,843 --> 00:38:27,397
[Actress Oh Ha Na]
<i>I'm here.</i>

565
00:38:27,397 --> 00:38:29,142
<i>Action!</i>

566
00:38:32,609 --> 00:38:33,968
- What?
- What?

567
00:38:33,968 --> 00:38:36,133
- You can't just come in here.
- Who are you?

568
00:38:36,133 --> 00:38:38,384
- Isn't that a rifle?
- Excuse me.

569
00:38:41,255 --> 00:38:42,924
Jeez, can't you see I'm in a meeting...

570
00:38:42,924 --> 00:38:45,345
- My comrades!
- Nan Young?

571
00:38:45,345 --> 00:38:47,889
She actually came dressed like that?

572
00:38:47,889 --> 00:38:50,002
<i>This is no time to sit around!</i>

573
00:38:50,002 --> 00:38:55,621
<i>Nothing will change if we simply sit back
and discuss the situation at hand.</i>

574
00:38:55,621 --> 00:39:01,142
<i>Do you know what I thought
after I blew up Wolhajeong?</i>

575
00:39:01,142 --> 00:39:03,647
<i>"I have nowhere left to return to.</i>

576
00:39:03,647 --> 00:39:06,248
<i>I could only move forward.</i>

577
00:39:06,248 --> 00:39:08,626
<i>Sorrow is temporary...</i>

578
00:39:09,912 --> 00:39:12,892
<i>But joy lasts forever."</i>

579
00:39:24,238 --> 00:39:25,893
<i>That's right, Comrade Nan Young.</i>

580
00:39:25,893 --> 00:39:29,145
<i>Let's march toward independence together.</i>

581
00:39:37,196 --> 00:39:39,296
Why did you show up only now?

582
00:39:39,296 --> 00:39:43,060
Just like you said, Ha Na,
it felt like Na Young was alive again.

583
00:39:48,974 --> 00:39:50,874
Director Ju Yi Jae?

584
00:39:51,508 --> 00:39:53,139
Director?

585
00:39:54,112 --> 00:39:55,695
Yeah...

586
00:40:00,673 --> 00:40:05,357
I've also prepared Scene 34. May I continue?

587
00:40:05,357 --> 00:40:08,891
Ms. Oh Ha Na, what exactly are you doing?

588
00:40:08,891 --> 00:40:12,108
I'm confident I can play Na Young really well.

589
00:40:12,108 --> 00:40:15,493
- Please give me the chance! I'm begging you!
- Yes...

590
00:40:15,493 --> 00:40:17,325
You were good.

591
00:40:17,325 --> 00:40:20,161
But it was the same performance
I've always seen from you.

592
00:40:20,161 --> 00:40:22,695
I mean, it wasn't anything special.

593
00:40:24,205 --> 00:40:25,585
Then...

594
00:40:25,585 --> 00:40:30,972
may I tell you why you should
choose me specifically?

595
00:40:30,972 --> 00:40:33,148
Oh? I'd like to hear this.

596
00:40:35,289 --> 00:40:37,110
I...

597
00:40:38,286 --> 00:40:42,372
I know someone
whose life is just like Nan Young's.

598
00:40:42,372 --> 00:40:48,302
A child who only did what they were told,
never dreaming for themselves...

599
00:40:50,188 --> 00:40:54,400
Never even realizing
their whole world was just a tiny prison.

600
00:40:55,099 --> 00:40:59,856
Then I met someone like Moo Gyeom and realized.

601
00:41:01,008 --> 00:41:04,798
<i>Here, you shoot the next take.</i>

602
00:41:07,195 --> 00:41:10,437
"Maybe if I break out of my little world,

603
00:41:10,437 --> 00:41:13,216
there's a much bigger one waiting for me."

604
00:41:13,216 --> 00:41:18,101
"I wanted to live in the same world as him."

605
00:41:19,615 --> 00:41:25,320
So they blew up their own little world
and ran out of it.

606
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:27,349
I...

607
00:41:27,349 --> 00:41:30,817
walked away from Topline Entertainment.

608
00:41:30,817 --> 00:41:33,299
I don't have an agency now,

609
00:41:33,299 --> 00:41:36,054
and I plan to keep going on my own.

610
00:41:36,054 --> 00:41:40,803
I also personally asked
Director Ju Yi Jae for this script.

611
00:41:40,803 --> 00:41:41,849
Oh...

612
00:41:41,849 --> 00:41:45,295
Then CEO An has no idea about any of this?

613
00:41:45,295 --> 00:41:47,367
She doesn't.

614
00:41:50,863 --> 00:41:53,253
So...

615
00:41:53,253 --> 00:41:55,150
even if I get the part,

616
00:41:55,150 --> 00:41:59,841
I'd like to keep it hidden
until filming starts.

617
00:41:59,841 --> 00:42:03,162
I'm sorry. Please help me...

618
00:42:03,162 --> 00:42:08,097
So I can live as Oh Ha Na, not her daughter.

619
00:42:10,808 --> 00:42:14,246
If Nan Young can be
my first step toward independence,

620
00:42:14,246 --> 00:42:17,409
it'll mean everything to me.

621
00:42:18,727 --> 00:42:23,802
After all, Nan Young's independence
has a happy ending.

622
00:42:27,673 --> 00:42:31,883
Could you wait outside for a moment?

623
00:42:42,778 --> 00:42:45,708
Sorry to keep you waiting. Please have a seat.

624
00:42:56,299 --> 00:42:58,084
Ms. Oh Ha Na.

625
00:43:01,832 --> 00:43:03,635
Let's do this together.

626
00:43:03,635 --> 00:43:06,112
I'm counting on you as our Nan Young.

627
00:43:08,160 --> 00:43:10,868
Oh, thank you.

628
00:43:10,868 --> 00:43:15,594
I'll do my absolute best
to become the best Nan Young I can.

629
00:43:15,594 --> 00:43:17,662
Do you know...

630
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:21,361
why I rejected you before?

631
00:43:21,361 --> 00:43:22,957
Well, that's because...

632
00:43:22,957 --> 00:43:26,114
my English wasn't good enough.

633
00:43:26,114 --> 00:43:30,091
The biggest reason was your attitude, Ha Na.

634
00:43:30,791 --> 00:43:36,791
You looked like a kid dragged there by her mom.

635
00:43:37,532 --> 00:43:39,307
Oh...

636
00:43:39,307 --> 00:43:41,911
I knew I couldn't fool a director's eyes.

637
00:43:41,911 --> 00:43:44,537
But today was different.

638
00:43:45,143 --> 00:43:49,229
You were impressive...
and it made me excited to work with you.

639
00:43:51,197 --> 00:43:53,230
Thank you.

640
00:43:54,674 --> 00:43:56,241
Well, anyway,

641
00:43:56,241 --> 00:44:00,196
from now on, we'll contact you directly.

642
00:44:00,196 --> 00:44:02,088
Keeping this confidential is our top priority.

643
00:44:02,088 --> 00:44:04,539
So don't tell your co-star either.

644
00:44:04,539 --> 00:44:06,855
Oh, right. Moo Gyeom!

645
00:44:06,855 --> 00:44:09,131
So is he someone I know?

646
00:44:09,131 --> 00:44:10,935
Who is it?

647
00:44:22,849 --> 00:44:25,685
- I told you not to come...
- Why?

648
00:44:25,685 --> 00:44:27,292
Why did you do it?

649
00:44:27,292 --> 00:44:29,932
Why did you sign a contract with my mom?

650
00:44:32,524 --> 00:44:34,910
Because I have to become someone.

651
00:44:35,997 --> 00:44:38,232
So please...

652
00:44:38,232 --> 00:44:41,005
stay away from me.

653
00:44:42,492 --> 00:44:44,630
That contract...

654
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:49,120
came with a promise that I'd never

655
00:44:49,977 --> 00:44:52,451
fall in love with you.

656
00:44:54,981 --> 00:44:56,881
That's a lie.

657
00:44:59,156 --> 00:45:01,131
No way...

658
00:45:01,131 --> 00:45:04,035
What kind of contract is that?

659
00:45:04,035 --> 00:45:06,528
Did you ever...

660
00:45:06,528 --> 00:45:08,891
love me, Yu Geon?

661
00:45:11,650 --> 00:45:13,383
No.

662
00:45:14,567 --> 00:45:16,525
Then why?

663
00:45:18,609 --> 00:45:21,447
What did we even have between us?

664
00:45:23,316 --> 00:45:25,216
You're right...

665
00:45:26,853 --> 00:45:29,641
What exactly was there between us?

666
00:45:32,409 --> 00:45:34,959
Because I know there wasn't
anything on my side.

667
00:45:50,574 --> 00:45:52,709
You're right.

668
00:45:52,709 --> 00:45:55,921
Friends are supposed to be alike.

669
00:46:01,965 --> 00:46:04,739
I misjudged you.

670
00:46:43,656 --> 00:46:45,449
[Moo Gyeom]

671
00:46:45,449 --> 00:46:48,536
[At the end of the hallway,
Moo Gyeom comes into view among the crowd]

672
00:46:48,536 --> 00:46:49,955
[Hair tied in a topknot, robe strings loosened]

673
00:46:49,955 --> 00:46:51,970
[Commanding presence, confident movements.
No shaky hands]

674
00:47:00,286 --> 00:47:02,186
Yeah, Dad.

675
00:47:06,137 --> 00:47:07,700
I'm here.

676
00:47:07,700 --> 00:47:09,756
You're here?

677
00:47:09,756 --> 00:47:12,353
Why are you here by yourself?
Where's Ju Young Jae?

678
00:47:12,353 --> 00:47:14,706
I sent him to the market.

679
00:47:21,387 --> 00:47:22,993
Here.

680
00:47:24,205 --> 00:47:26,682
- What is it?
- Make this delivery first.

681
00:47:26,682 --> 00:47:28,957
The address is attached.

682
00:47:37,963 --> 00:47:39,917
Delivery.

683
00:47:43,870 --> 00:47:46,051
- Soo Bin?
- Yeah.

684
00:47:46,051 --> 00:47:47,413
Come in.

685
00:47:47,413 --> 00:47:48,789
What are you doing here?

686
00:47:48,789 --> 00:47:51,637
I asked your dad to arrange this.

687
00:47:51,637 --> 00:47:52,689
Huh?

688
00:47:52,689 --> 00:47:55,314
[CEO: Seo In Uk, Open Frame Works,
Actress, Name: Oh Ha Na]

689
00:47:55,314 --> 00:47:58,297
- I look forward to working with you.
- Me too.

690
00:47:58,297 --> 00:48:00,240
Oh, you're here?

691
00:48:02,595 --> 00:48:04,477
You're here?

692
00:48:05,194 --> 00:48:06,693
You two know each other?

693
00:48:06,693 --> 00:48:10,329
Yes, we knew each other. In the past...

694
00:48:10,329 --> 00:48:12,990
Oh, because of "Contract Marriage?"

695
00:48:12,990 --> 00:48:15,223
We were the lead and Extra No. 1,

696
00:48:15,223 --> 00:48:17,374
weren't we?

697
00:48:17,374 --> 00:48:18,682
What's going on here?

698
00:48:18,682 --> 00:48:20,486
We're here for the script reading.

699
00:48:20,486 --> 00:48:24,924
Say hello. That's Nan Young,
and he's Moo Gyeom.

700
00:48:24,924 --> 00:48:29,279
- What?
- Did Moo Gyeom sign the contract yet?

701
00:48:29,279 --> 00:48:32,217
Oh, maybe my mom signed it on your behalf, huh?

702
00:48:32,217 --> 00:48:35,635
Right... did you?

703
00:48:35,635 --> 00:48:39,013
That didn't sound like a question.

704
00:48:48,152 --> 00:48:50,058
Scene 47. Street. Night.

705
00:48:50,058 --> 00:48:55,109
"In the midst of it all, Na Young and
Moo Gyeom walk in, dressed in suits.

706
00:48:55,109 --> 00:48:58,067
Unlike the noise around them,
the two walk at a slow pace."

707
00:48:58,067 --> 00:49:00,898
"No matter how I look at you,
I see not a trace of worry."

708
00:49:00,898 --> 00:49:02,558
"How is it?

709
00:49:02,558 --> 00:49:07,337
Not Wolhajeong's lanterns,
but this moonlight reveals my beauty."

710
00:49:07,337 --> 00:49:10,271
"How is it that you find everything a jest?"

711
00:49:10,271 --> 00:49:13,957
To "Gyeongseong Love Song!"

712
00:49:21,903 --> 00:49:24,733
Oh, you two are so awkward.

713
00:49:24,733 --> 00:49:28,074
You're about to fall in love.
How about getting a little friendlier?

714
00:49:28,074 --> 00:49:31,070
I'd love that.

715
00:49:31,070 --> 00:49:33,859
But I'm just not sure if Yu Geon can.

716
00:49:33,859 --> 00:49:37,631
He seems cold, but he's a genuinely good guy.

717
00:49:37,631 --> 00:49:39,213
Really?

718
00:49:39,213 --> 00:49:42,778
I guess you're very different on the inside
than you are on the outside.

719
00:49:43,973 --> 00:49:48,121
Neither of you was bad,
but you barely looked at each other.

720
00:49:48,121 --> 00:49:49,786
Even if it's just a reading,

721
00:49:49,786 --> 00:49:52,534
you need to make eye contact
and build chemistry.

722
00:49:52,534 --> 00:49:55,778
If you're just going to read separately,
you could've done that at home.

723
00:49:56,419 --> 00:49:57,564
I'm sorry.

724
00:49:57,564 --> 00:49:59,242
I'm sorry.

725
00:49:59,242 --> 00:50:01,444
But that's what made it fascinating.

726
00:50:01,444 --> 00:50:04,430
How did you have such natural back-and-forth
without even looking at each other?

727
00:50:04,430 --> 00:50:06,785
Did you two have a falling-out or something?

728
00:50:13,902 --> 00:50:15,659
Guess I was right.

729
00:50:15,659 --> 00:50:17,742
Huh? They have to be friends first
to have a falling-out.

730
00:50:17,742 --> 00:50:19,660
I've seen those two together before.

731
00:50:19,660 --> 00:50:22,267
- They seemed pretty close.
- Oh, really?

732
00:50:22,267 --> 00:50:24,984
If the friendship's over,

733
00:50:24,984 --> 00:50:26,749
maybe it's time to fall in love instead.

734
00:50:26,749 --> 00:50:30,799
This is a romance.
You can't act like sworn enemies.

735
00:50:30,799 --> 00:50:32,971
Once the cameras roll, it'll be different.

736
00:50:32,971 --> 00:50:36,305
Love will be even harder.

737
00:50:36,305 --> 00:50:38,446
You tell me.

738
00:50:39,164 --> 00:50:41,600
Can you love me?

739
00:50:49,446 --> 00:50:53,090
I have to. The directors told us to.

740
00:50:53,090 --> 00:50:55,209
What about you, Ha Na?

741
00:50:55,875 --> 00:51:00,694
If it helps the project,
I'll do whatever it takes.

742
00:51:01,314 --> 00:51:03,747
That's disappointing.

743
00:51:03,747 --> 00:51:06,326
I'm already in love.

744
00:51:14,805 --> 00:51:17,128
There's definitely something going on.

745
00:51:17,128 --> 00:51:19,795
- I'm dying to know. Right?
- Not really.

746
00:51:19,795 --> 00:51:23,186
Hey, I've never seen
Yu Geon look like that before.

747
00:51:23,186 --> 00:51:24,539
How should I put it...

748
00:51:24,539 --> 00:51:27,201
His eyes looked cold, yet... sad?

749
00:51:27,201 --> 00:51:29,567
Looks more like a breakup than a falling-out.

750
00:51:29,567 --> 00:51:32,390
That's good. It means
they've already been in love.

751
00:51:32,390 --> 00:51:33,841
What? Seriously?

752
00:51:33,841 --> 00:51:36,336
Then the emotions should come naturally.

753
00:51:36,336 --> 00:51:38,666
Should we shoot the breakup scene first?

754
00:51:38,666 --> 00:51:44,774
Wow... that was a terrible thing to say.

755
00:51:44,774 --> 00:51:47,323
Don't worry so much.

756
00:51:47,323 --> 00:51:50,101
On set, those feelings will slip out
whether they want them to or not.

757
00:51:50,101 --> 00:51:53,071
All we have to do is catch it and bring it out.

758
00:51:53,071 --> 00:51:57,788
Then maybe a love
that's like a war is better, right?

759
00:51:57,788 --> 00:52:02,110
I always wrote better in intense relationships
than peaceful ones.

760
00:52:02,110 --> 00:52:05,131
Probably because the emotions run deeper...

761
00:52:06,949 --> 00:52:08,200
When?

762
00:52:08,200 --> 00:52:09,588
Huh?

763
00:52:11,585 --> 00:52:14,835
I mean... back in college.
Most people date a classmate at least once.

764
00:52:14,835 --> 00:52:16,684
I didn't.

765
00:52:17,523 --> 00:52:19,528
Really?

766
00:52:19,528 --> 00:52:22,209
Come on, that's the perfect age for it.

767
00:52:22,209 --> 00:52:23,444
So what were you doing?

768
00:52:23,444 --> 00:52:26,020
Busy hauling equipment around on set.

769
00:52:26,020 --> 00:52:28,685
I'd buy one baguette
and make it last a whole week.

770
00:52:28,685 --> 00:52:33,111
Okay, enough! Skip it!
Is that even love at that age?

771
00:52:36,213 --> 00:52:38,315
Then what were we back then?

772
00:52:41,762 --> 00:52:44,827
When we were 18 and 19...

773
00:52:44,827 --> 00:52:46,746
what were we back then?

774
00:52:55,651 --> 00:52:57,756
It was love.

775
00:52:58,363 --> 00:53:01,820
Back then, too... When we were 18 and 19.

776
00:53:04,470 --> 00:53:06,578
And I think...

777
00:53:07,751 --> 00:53:10,001
it still is.

778
00:53:25,961 --> 00:53:28,190
I know everything.

779
00:53:28,190 --> 00:53:31,900
I know you accepted Yu Geon to protect me.

780
00:53:38,511 --> 00:53:41,028
- Yi Jae...
- I'm not blaming you.

781
00:53:41,028 --> 00:53:43,282
I don't blame you anymore.

782
00:53:43,894 --> 00:53:48,732
I just... kept wondering

783
00:53:48,732 --> 00:53:51,538
what kind of feeling that must've been.

784
00:53:52,604 --> 00:53:56,342
They say all great things begin
with something small.

785
00:53:56,342 --> 00:54:01,813
Just like loving me made you love filmmaking.

786
00:54:02,928 --> 00:54:05,187
But...

787
00:54:05,187 --> 00:54:07,993
isn't that feeling itself

788
00:54:07,993 --> 00:54:10,542
what makes it truly great?

789
00:54:10,542 --> 00:54:13,110
Even the heart...

790
00:54:13,110 --> 00:54:15,370
that made you decide to stop.

791
00:54:22,046 --> 00:54:24,575
Your heart is too big for me

792
00:54:24,575 --> 00:54:27,873
to keep pretending I don't see it, Woo Soo Bin.

793
00:54:30,005 --> 00:54:31,837
So...

794
00:54:33,530 --> 00:54:35,430
don't stop.

795
00:55:19,266 --> 00:55:22,929
I'm already so nervous. What should I do?

796
00:55:22,929 --> 00:55:26,261
Even legendary directors get nervous
the night before their first shoot.

797
00:55:26,261 --> 00:55:27,274
Yeah?

798
00:55:27,274 --> 00:55:29,652
- That's why I come here the day before...
- Yeah.

799
00:55:29,652 --> 00:55:33,906
and run through everything in my head.

800
00:55:33,906 --> 00:55:35,286
How?

801
00:55:35,286 --> 00:55:36,723
Look.

802
00:55:36,723 --> 00:55:40,982
The first thing you'll notice
is probably the art department.

803
00:55:40,982 --> 00:55:44,237
- Yeah.
- They'll check all the signs again

804
00:55:45,583 --> 00:55:50,122
and set up the gukbap place nicely,
with the soup steaming.

805
00:55:50,122 --> 00:55:51,602
- Over there, Director of Photography...
- Yeah.

806
00:55:51,602 --> 00:55:55,450
will be waiting with gummies,
wondering when the setup will be finished.

807
00:55:55,450 --> 00:55:58,880
Yes, Assistant Director! I'm on my way!

808
00:55:59,754 --> 00:56:02,102
On set, always watch where you're stepping.

809
00:56:02,102 --> 00:56:04,720
Tripping over a cable can be a disaster.

810
00:56:04,720 --> 00:56:08,287
And stay out of the lighting crew's way.

811
00:57:12,784 --> 00:57:14,421
Yi Jae!

812
00:57:18,403 --> 00:57:20,642
And this...

813
00:57:20,642 --> 00:57:23,153
Director Ju Yi Jae, this is your spot.

814
00:57:23,153 --> 00:57:24,789
[Director Ju Yi Jae]

815
00:57:44,314 --> 00:57:46,771
[Director Ju Yi Jae]

816
00:57:50,121 --> 00:57:53,291
Sit here and call it out as loud as you can,

817
00:57:53,291 --> 00:57:57,389
"Ready... Action!"

818
00:57:57,389 --> 00:57:59,534
- Me?
- Yeah.

819
00:57:59,534 --> 00:58:03,514
[Director Woo Soo Bin, Director Ju Yi Jae]

820
00:58:03,514 --> 00:58:08,298
Everyone will be waiting for your cue.

821
00:58:11,305 --> 00:58:12,941
Go ahead.

822
00:58:24,195 --> 00:58:26,179
Ready...

823
00:58:34,448 --> 00:58:36,118
Action!

824
00:59:08,814 --> 00:59:10,006
[No Dating on Set]
<i>Directors,</i>

825
00:59:10,006 --> 00:59:12,620
<i>if you ever catch the staff dating,
report it to us right away.</i>

826
00:59:12,620 --> 00:59:16,098
<i>You should've stayed right by my side
and shown my mom properly.</i>

827
00:59:16,098 --> 00:59:17,745
<i>That there's absolutely no such thing as love.</i>

828
00:59:17,745 --> 00:59:18,897
<i>Relax.</i>

829
00:59:18,897 --> 00:59:21,406
<i>Oh Ha Na! Everyone, stop filming!</i>

830
00:59:21,406 --> 00:59:22,727
<i>I'll withdraw from the project, CEO An.</i>

831
00:59:22,727 --> 00:59:25,798
<i>It all happened because of
that stupid rebellious attitude of yours.</i>

832
00:59:25,798 --> 00:59:27,975
<i>I'm sorry. Because of me...</i>

833
00:59:27,975 --> 00:59:30,104
<i>I shouldn't have tried to fix you.</i>

834
00:59:30,104 --> 00:59:34,770
<i>Things that are broken once
are hard to fix completely.</i>

835
00:59:34,770 --> 00:59:36,493
<i>Yi Jae!</i>

